\f0 \cf0 \pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
{\*\bkmkstart C_albicans_Biology}Candida{\*\bkmkend C_albicans_Biology} albicans
\f1\i0  is the most common cause of invasive candidiasis, a bloodstream and deep-organ infection with a global incidence of roughly 3-5 cases per 100,000 people per year, affecting up to 2% of ICU admissions and carrying a mortality rate of up to 40% despite anti-fungal therapies \{Pappas et al., "Invasive candidiasis", 2018\}. In the Netherlands, roughly 445 candidemia cases, 239 cases of 
\f2\i Candida
\f1\i0  peritonitis per year, and recurrent vulvovaginal candidiasis affecting an estimated 220,000 women annually have placed a severe burden on the healthcare system \{Buil et al., "Burden of serious fungal infections in the Netherlands", 2020\}. \
In the commensal form, 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  cells exhibit a roundish yeast morphology. Environment factors such as high temperature, hypoxia, starvation, serum type, and growing on solid surfaces can trigger apical growth of 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  into an elongated hyphal form capable of invasion. The growth starts by extending a germ tube at the site marked by polarity landmark proteins such as such as Int1 and Rsr1 and is driven by the turgor pressure, created by intracellular osmotic gradients. A complex system of vesicle synthesis, transport to the tip along actin filaments, and delivery to the growing tip by the Spitzenk\'f6rper sustains the continuous growth. Notably, the entire hypha does not exist as a single cell but a chain of compartments. The cells undergo mitosis without cell separation, and as the tip grows, septa gradually form behind to close the cell body into distinct compartments. Invasion of the tip into the host cell can happen through three mechanisms: turgor pressure-driven active penetration, enzymatic degradation of the host cell membrane, and induced endocytosis triggered in the host cell when adhesins such as Als3 bind epithelial cadherins and EGFR \{Brown et al., "Stress adaptation in a pathogenic fungus", 2014; Desai, "Candida albicans Hyphae: From Growth Initiation to Invasion", 2018; Thomson et al., "High frame-rate resolution of cell division during Candida albicans filamentation", 2016\}.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 {\*\bkmkstart Coculture_and_smFISH}Despite{\*\bkmkend Coculture_and_smFISH} the prevalence of 
\f2\i Candida
\f1\i0  infections, the invasion mechanism itself is understood mainly through single-gene knockouts and bulk population assays \{Fan et al., "Hyphae-Specific Genes HGC1, ALS3, HWP1, and ECE1 and Relevant Signaling Pathways in Candida albicans", 2013; Nobile et al., "Function of Candida albicans adhesin hwp1 in biofilm formation", 2006; Moyes et al., "Candidalysin is a fungal peptide toxin critical for mucosal infection", 2016\}. While they have identified several key factors governing the invasion process, they cannot show how transcript localization, mechanical penetration, adhesion, and membrane damage are coordinated in time and space within a single invading hypha. Elucidating such coordination could reveal rate-limiting steps for invasion and potential targets for new anti-fungal strategies.  \
Therefore, a model system that captures fungal and host interaction during the invasion and analytical methods capable of detecting single cell and single molecule gene expression patterns are needed. To this end, a co-culture was established between human gingival epithelial cells and 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  cells, and single molecule fluorescence in situ hybridization (smFISH) was used to detect mRNAs of key genes for hyphal growth and invasion. smFISH works by hybridizing multiple short, fluorescently labeled oligonucleotide probes along a single target mRNA, and their combined signal appears as one diffraction-limited spot per transcript \{Otterdijk et al., "Single-Molecule Fluorescent In Situ Hybridization (smFISH) for RNA Detection in the Fungal Pathogen Candida albicans", 2024\}. Individual mRNA molecules can be counted and localized within a cell, connecting the cell-scale invasion mechanics to the patterns of transcript production and localization that drive them.\
In this project, 5 genes have been probed with smFISH. SHE3 is an mRNA-localization factor that, by analogy to its role in budding yeast, is thought to help traffic transcripts toward the growing tip; CLB2 is a cell cycle cyclin whose mRNA has been reported to concentrate near the hyphal apex, coupling cell cycle progression to polarized extension; ECE1 encodes the precursor of the toxin candidalysin, and its deletion leaves germ-tube formation intact but shortens hyphae by roughly 50%; ALS3 is an adhesin that mediates host-cell binding and biofilm scaffolding, with a ~60% loss of epithelial adhesion in its absence \{Fan et al., "Hyphae-Specific Genes HGC1, ALS3, HWP1, and ECE1 and Relevant Signaling Pathways in Candida albicans", 2013\}; HWP1 is a hypha-specific adhesin that cross-links to host transglutaminases, and its deletion reduces epithelial adherence by ~70% and biofilm dry mass three-fold \{Nobile et al., "Function of Candida albicans adhesin hwp1 in biofilm formation", 2006\}.\
Besides smFISH, fluorescence staining was used to detect intracellular structures. DAPI staining was used to image both 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  and epithelial nuclei. Calcofluor bound to the cell walls and septa of the hyphal cells. Phalloidin is a dye that enters epithelial cells and binds actin molecules. When a hyphal cell penetrates into the epithelial cell, actin molecules aggregate around it. Hence, phalloidin staining acted as an indicator for hyphal invasion. Differential Interference Contrast (DIC) microscopy was also used to visualize the morphologies of the hyphal cells and epithelial cells.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\*\bkmkstart Existing_cell_segmentation}Extracting{\*\bkmkend Existing_cell_segmentation} quantitative measurements from the multi-modal imaging data first requires instance segmentation, where each cell is segmented with a separate mask. Several deep learning approaches have been developed for instance segmentation. The ones tested or applied in this project follow the U-Net design with an encoder and a decoder. Broadly, the encoders are based either on convolutional or vision transformer (ViT) architectures. Convolutional encoders typically include several convolutional layers that each slides a fix-sized learned convolution operator along the image to gradually downsample the image into a compact latent space representation containing the meaningful information. ViT encoders also extract the latent representation but by treating image patches as sequences and use self-attention to capture the long-range dependencies in the image instead. In either case, a convolutional decoder then upsamples from the latent representation to segment the cells \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\{Hatamizadeh et al., "UNETR: Transformers for 3D Medical Image Segmentation", 2021\}, \{Li et al., "Exploring Plain Vision Transformer Backbones for Object Detection", 2022\}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 . As the cell labels are integers in arbitrary orders, the models do not predict the masks directly but reconstruct them from predicted cell probabilities and distance fields, which represent a pixel\'92s distance to the cell boundary or center. \
Several U-nets have been specifically trained on large microscopy image datasets. Among them, Cellpose predicts a cell probability map and a field of vectors pointing towards the cell centers. The masks are built by \'93flowing\'94 the pixels with a high cell probability along their vector directions until they converge\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\{Stringer et al., "Cellpose: a generalist algorithm for cellular segmentation", 2021\}. \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Omnipose replaces Cellpose's center-seeking flow field with a flow field that points towards the medial axis of cells, correcting Cellpose\'92s tendency to fail on elongated cells \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\{Cutler et al., "Omnipose: a high-precision morphology-independent solution for bacterial cell segmentation", 2022\}. Both Cellpose and Omnipose use convolutional encoders. Th Segment Anything Model (SAM) is a vision foundational model trained for automatic and prompted instance segmentation on general life images. Its architecture consists of a ViT encoder and a mask decoder \{Kirillov et al., "Segment Anything", 2023\}. Cellpose-SAM \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 finetunes the ViT encoder of SAM on microscopy data and combines it with Cellpose's flow-based decoder to achieve broad generalization across cell morphologies \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\{Pachitariu et al., "Cellpose-SAM: superhuman generalization for cellular segmentation", 2025\}. Segment anything for microscopy (\uc0\u956 SAM) is also based on finetuning the SAM encoder and uses a convolutional decoder to predict a cell probability map, a center distance map, and a boundary distance map for mask reconstruction \{Archit et al., "Segment Anything for Microscopy", 2025\}.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\*\bkmkstart Challenges_in_analyzing_cocult}Although{\*\bkmkend Challenges_in_analyzing_cocult} these models perform well for generic microscopy images, their flow field and cell probability representation of cell morphologies assume cells are roundish or only mildly elongated, morphologically similar to one another, and spatially non-overlapping. None of these assumptions hold for our co-culture of invading 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  and epithelial cells: hyphal cells grow as long, thin filaments, epithelial cells migrate leading to highly irregular outlines, and the two cell types overlap one another over the course of infection. This means that the same cell will have disjointed flow fields, leading to over-segmentation.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 {\*\bkmkstart Previous_network_segmentation_}Particularly{\*\bkmkend Previous_network_segmentation_}, overlapping hyphal cells form a network that requires reconstructing the network topology from the imaging data to disentangle the individual hyphal cells. One earlier paper reconstructed fungal networks by applying a classical Frangi vesselness filter on the image then using a minimum spanning tree gap filling step to reconnect fragmented detections \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\{Saponaro et al., "Three-Dimensional Segmentation of Vesicular Networks of Fungal Hyphae in Macroscopic Microscopy Image Stacks", 2017\}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 . However, this approach is not directly transferrable for this project as our hyphal cells are imaged at a higher magnification, which introduces morphological features and noises that the Frangi filter cannot handle. Also, hyphal cells do not always connect in a way that forms a minimum spanning tree.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
{\*\bkmkstart Scene_Graph_Generation}Beyond{\*\bkmkend Scene_Graph_Generation} pixel-level segmentation, downstream modeling of cell-cell interactions benefits from representing cell-cell relationships in a graph structure with nodes being detected cells and edges being their relations. {\*\atrfstart 1}\f1\fs24\b0\i0\ul0 In this project\'92s context, the nodes are healthy epithelial cells, invaded epithelial cells, and hyphal cells, while the edges are invading or non-invading.{\*\atrfend 1}\f1\fs24\b0\i0\ul0 {{\*\atnid Chuyao Wang}{\*\atnauthor Chuyao Wang}\chatn{\*\annotation{\*\atnref 1}\pard\plain\f1\fs24\b0\i0\ul0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Chuyao Wang 6/19/26, 21:57 Depending on progress in the last month\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
}}\f1\fs24\b0\i0\ul0  Besides these, the nodes can also be over-segmented cell masks, and the edges encode whether they belong to the same cell. Extracting such graphs from the imaging data is a scene graph generation (SGG) task, involving not only cell segmentation but also cell (node) classification and relation (edge) classification.\
SGG methods fall into one-stage or two-stage categories. Two-stage methods first detect and classify objects with an object detector then train a separate relation prediction model on these fixed detections, whereas one-stage methods train detection and relation prediction jointly, allowing the two tasks to inform each other during optimization \{Chang et al., "A Comprehensive Survey of Scene Graphs: Generation and Application", 2022\}. Although the one-stage approach is cleaner, learning a joint representation for both tasks is more difficult with limited data, while the two-stage approach allows us to take advantage of the existing instance segmentation models for cell segmentation and visual feature extraction, keeping node and edge classification a separate task. Also, since we only have a very small number set of node and edge types, this greatly reduces the complexity of the second task.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\*\bkmkstart Thesis_Objective_Invasion_dete}Therefore{\*\bkmkend Thesis_Objective_Invasion_dete}, the aim of this project is to build a two-stage computer vision pipeline that processes microscopy images of the co-culture. In the first stage, an instance segmentation model is used to predict masks of epithelial and 
\f2\i C. albicans
\f1\i0  that could be over-segmented, and the second stage classifies the cells into cell types and builds a scene graph that can be used to join the over-segmented cells and represent the invasion relationship between epithelial and hyphal cells.\
\pard\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\fi720\sl480\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
